WEBVTT

01:45.930 --> 01:46.790
What do you think?

01:47.230 --> 01:53.350
I tried changing the melody to match
the lyrics the two of you wrote.

01:53.350 --> 01:54.910
It's fantastic.

01:54.910 --> 02:00.670
It was great before, but the changes
have made it even more brilliant.

02:01.750 --> 02:02.930
That's great.

02:02.930 --> 02:08.000
The two of us will now train together
to make this the finest of songs.

02:08.590 --> 02:09.980
Not enough.

02:09.490 --> 02:09.980
What?

02:10.320 --> 02:11.860
What's not enough?

02:12.890 --> 02:14.980
I don't know.

02:15.600 --> 02:16.940
I see.

02:16.940 --> 02:21.740
But let's work diligently
to fill whatever holes are left.

02:22.990 --> 02:25.120
I look forward to hearing you sing.

02:25.700 --> 02:29.830
The two of you have a similar
feel to you, don't you?

02:29.830 --> 02:32.030
I've been sensing the same thing.

02:32.510 --> 02:35.420
It feels like I've met him before.

02:35.740 --> 02:38.860
My family is from Kochi.

02:38.860 --> 02:43.330
What? You're a member
of the Sumeragi family of Tosa?

02:45.850 --> 02:49.600
The Sumeragi family is
an old family that has had dealings

02:49.600 --> 02:51.830
with the Hijirikawa family.

02:51.830 --> 02:52.630
What?

02:52.630 --> 02:58.110
I've never met any of them before,
but it does mean our bond runs deep.

02:58.960 --> 03:01.780
Is your family understanding of your musical activities?

03:02.910 --> 03:06.040
My father told me to follow my own path.

03:07.070 --> 03:08.460
I see.

03:13.170 --> 03:14.630
I was so surprised.

03:14.630 --> 03:18.440
I had no idea you two
were connected in that way.

03:18.440 --> 03:19.130
Yeah.

03:19.970 --> 03:22.680
Starting tomorrow, the two of us

03:22.680 --> 03:26.140
will work diligently to create
lyrics worthy of your song.

03:26.140 --> 03:29.020
Okay. I'll work on the arrangement, too.

03:29.020 --> 03:29.780
Yeah.

03:33.560 --> 03:34.860
Missed Calls:     20

03:33.560 --> 03:34.860
Kyoto (Home)

03:39.370 --> 03:40.060
Hello.

03:40.060 --> 03:43.300
Masato-sama, this is your
father's secretary, Matsuyama.

03:43.300 --> 03:45.530
I'm sorry for calling so many times.

03:45.940 --> 03:48.110
I'm sorry I couldn't answer sooner.

03:48.520 --> 03:50.110
I was in the middle of work.

03:50.110 --> 03:53.880
It's fine. Please listen carefully.

03:54.530 --> 03:56.590
Your father has collapsed.

04:01.010 --> 04:03.380
Hijirikawa Masato

04:02.110 --> 04:03.380
Sumeragi-san,

04:03.380 --> 04:08.200
I'm terribly sorry, but I'd like
to postpone tomorrow morning's practice.

04:08.200 --> 04:08.990
What?

04:08.990 --> 04:11.770
I have to make a sudden trip to Kyoto.

04:11.770 --> 04:13.870
Your home?

04:13.870 --> 04:14.660
Yes.

04:19.690 --> 04:21.280
Sorry I'm late.

04:21.280 --> 04:22.320
What is that for?

04:23.250 --> 04:25.950
Once practice is over,
I'll be returning to Kyoto.

04:27.300 --> 04:28.370
My father collapsed.

04:28.370 --> 04:29.370
What?

04:33.910 --> 04:35.390
Is he okay?

04:35.390 --> 04:36.410
Yeah.

04:36.410 --> 04:40.290
He needs rest, but they say his condition is stable.

04:40.290 --> 04:41.920
That's good.

04:41.920 --> 04:44.340
So, are you okay?

04:45.620 --> 04:50.300
Your original agreement was to come
to Saotome Academy for only one year.

04:50.730 --> 04:54.350
It'll be your first time
going back home since then.

04:56.350 --> 04:58.220
Don't worry about me.

04:58.220 --> 05:00.730
I'm not the man I used to be.

05:00.730 --> 05:03.730
Really? That's fine, then.

05:05.920 --> 05:07.460
There's no problem at all.

05:12.520 --> 05:14.290
I'll be back tomorrow night.

05:14.290 --> 05:15.630
See you later.

05:17.880 --> 05:20.710
I'm worried about his father.

05:20.710 --> 05:24.630
This is the first time we've
watched someone go back home.

05:26.510 --> 05:28.890
It's kind of a weird feeling, isn't it?

05:49.660 --> 05:52.080
Masato-sama, welcome home.

05:53.150 --> 05:54.670
I'm back.

05:54.670 --> 05:56.730
Sir!

05:56.730 --> 05:57.710
Fujikawa.

05:57.710 --> 05:59.170
It's been a while.

06:00.250 --> 06:01.660
Thank you...

06:01.660 --> 06:03.650
Thank you for making this decision!

06:04.250 --> 06:06.260
I heard the news from the master.

06:07.070 --> 06:10.930
I've always supported
your desire to pursue music.

06:10.930 --> 06:16.980
But if you've voluntarily chosen
to take over the Hijirikawa family,

06:16.980 --> 06:19.310
nothing could make me happier.

06:21.140 --> 06:22.900
Now we have nothing to worry about.

06:22.900 --> 06:24.440
What a fantastic decision.

06:24.440 --> 06:26.760
He's grown into such a magnificent young man.

06:30.270 --> 06:31.490
Are you all right?

06:31.490 --> 06:34.990
Yeah. The doctor said there's
nothing to worry about anymore.

06:35.460 --> 06:38.120
Everyone else is making too much of a fuss.

06:38.870 --> 06:40.490
That's good to hear.

06:42.000 --> 06:44.500
Don't you have something else you want to say?

06:46.930 --> 06:50.910
I never said I would take over the family.

06:50.910 --> 06:53.010
I only ever gave you a year.

06:54.470 --> 06:57.290
But I've kept my mouth shut
and allowed you to continue.

06:57.290 --> 06:59.070
I thought your experience

06:59.070 --> 07:02.770
in the entertainment industry would
someday benefit the Hijirikawa family.

07:03.170 --> 07:04.550
Wait, I—

07:04.550 --> 07:06.050
Haven't you had enough?

07:06.050 --> 07:08.970
As the eldest son of the Hijirikawa family

07:09.450 --> 07:12.330
that has written history for generations,

07:12.330 --> 07:14.600
you have a responsibility
to continue our traditions.

07:16.400 --> 07:20.640
Tens of thousands of employees
work for the Hijirikawa Conglomerate,

07:20.640 --> 07:24.460
and they're all looking forward to when you take over.

07:24.770 --> 07:30.550
By sticking to your own desires,
you could be depriving them all of employment.

07:34.470 --> 07:37.510
You should obediently do as I say.

07:37.910 --> 07:39.810
You'll understand someday.

07:41.680 --> 07:47.220
But STARISH is trying to qualify
for the Triple S decisive concert.

07:47.220 --> 07:48.410
It's an important time for us.

07:48.410 --> 07:50.160
Then all the more reason to do it now.

07:50.860 --> 07:52.190
Don't you understand?

07:52.760 --> 07:56.470
The more important you become
in the world of STARISH,

07:56.470 --> 07:59.830
the more you will hurt them by leaving.

08:01.050 --> 08:04.740
To decide soon would be best for them, too.

08:04.740 --> 08:06.540
You must understand that.

08:08.330 --> 08:09.630
I...

08:12.260 --> 08:15.820
I came to check on you.

08:15.820 --> 08:18.030
We can discuss this another time.

08:18.490 --> 08:20.010
I'm going back to Tokyo tomorrow.

08:20.010 --> 08:21.020
You can't.

08:21.570 --> 08:24.870
The day after tomorrow,
we'll be holding the Banquet of Autumn Leaves.

08:24.870 --> 08:26.660
The Banquet of Autumn Leaves?

08:26.660 --> 08:28.560
As you know,

08:28.560 --> 08:33.580
it's an important event attended by
all members of the Hijirikawa family.

08:33.580 --> 08:35.990
But I can't attend.

08:36.330 --> 08:39.540
You must attend as my proxy.

08:39.540 --> 08:40.710
But...

08:40.710 --> 08:44.080
What is it? If you have something
to say, say it clearly.

08:49.190 --> 08:50.460
Nothing has changed.

08:52.170 --> 08:54.470
Not him, not me.

08:55.100 --> 08:58.100
The head of a family must make decisions.

08:58.680 --> 09:01.100
I don't know how to decide.

09:01.100 --> 09:03.140
You have to think about that for yourself.

09:04.900 --> 09:06.310
Pull yourself together.

09:06.310 --> 09:09.850
If you have something to say,
say it in your own words.

09:13.030 --> 09:16.650
The air here in this mansion is unchanged.

09:17.130 --> 09:19.110
Nothing has changed here.

09:21.580 --> 09:21.890
Otoya
Yeah.

09:21.580 --> 09:23.120
Sorry. I'm extending my stay in Kyoto by two days
I've made adjustments to my schedule

09:21.970 --> 09:23.120
Masato

09:27.500 --> 09:29.080
Sumeragi Kira-sama
I'd like to request that our practice session be postponed again.

09:34.220 --> 09:36.900
Yeah, apparently he's coming
back tomorrow night.

09:36.900 --> 09:40.800
Whatever the reason, if he went home,

09:40.800 --> 09:43.600
they're probably talking about whether
or not he'll take over the family business.

09:44.090 --> 09:45.520
Yeah.

09:45.520 --> 09:49.020
We're talking about Ma-kun here.
He'll probably be fine.

09:49.020 --> 09:50.900
But I'm a little worried.

09:50.900 --> 09:54.140
They have the decisive concert coming up.

09:54.140 --> 09:56.070
I just hope there aren't any problems.

09:56.070 --> 10:00.700
I know. Being the heir to a financial
conglomerate must be so hard.

10:00.700 --> 10:03.950
We can't even imagine what their world is like.

10:03.950 --> 10:06.370
Yeah, but it sure is a coincidence.

10:06.750 --> 10:08.610
We have three sons
from distinguished families.

10:08.610 --> 10:11.170
Well, one is of a formerly
distinguished family, I guess.

10:11.480 --> 10:17.040
The Kurosaki Conglomerate went
bankrupt when he was just a kid.

10:17.040 --> 10:20.360
The head of a conglomerate's
responsibility for his employees

10:20.360 --> 10:22.260
is a heavy burden to bear.

10:22.260 --> 10:25.100
I saw my father suffer.

10:25.100 --> 10:26.780
You're right.

10:26.780 --> 10:28.940
He's the eldest son of the Hijirikawa family.

10:29.310 --> 10:34.270
He was born to be the head of the family,
and carry the burden of that responsibility.

10:34.270 --> 10:38.490
In his world, he can't afford to choose.

10:38.490 --> 10:42.770
Yeah, but he's not who he used to be.

10:43.870 --> 10:47.310
He has new bonds now.

10:47.910 --> 10:50.500
An exceptionally powerful one called STARISH.

10:52.620 --> 10:53.660
Bonds...

10:58.230 --> 11:02.760
I thought continuing to pursue music
with my friends had made me stronger.

11:03.500 --> 11:08.100
I can't believe that, in actuality,
nothing has changed since I was a child.

11:11.850 --> 11:13.400
Excuse me.

11:13.400 --> 11:14.280
Fujikawa.

11:14.280 --> 11:16.550
Matsuyama told me.

11:16.550 --> 11:19.900
You only returned to check on your father.

11:19.900 --> 11:21.130
That's right.

11:23.100 --> 11:24.700
This piano brings back memories.

11:26.010 --> 11:29.450
When I was a child,
I was terrified of my father.

11:29.450 --> 11:32.450
I couldn't even eat while he was around.

11:33.100 --> 11:36.590
That's when you taught me how to play the piano.

11:39.350 --> 11:44.760
I made it through those days
because I had music as an escape.

11:46.590 --> 11:48.640
My father's feelings are strong.

11:49.490 --> 11:52.520
I couldn't say anything.

11:53.480 --> 11:57.700
But I don't want to quit STARISH.

12:04.030 --> 12:05.950
From: Nanami Haruka
To: Sumeragi Kira > Hijirikawa Masato
Duet Project
Hijirikawa-san, Sumeragi-san,
Thank you for all your hard work.
I've finished the arrangement for the duet project.
When you get the chance, please give it a listen.
You can download the song here.

12:09.320 --> 12:11.520
Sorry for interrupting you
while you're working.

12:11.520 --> 12:13.530
It's okay. We just finished.

12:14.250 --> 12:15.080
Well?

12:15.080 --> 12:20.000
Sumeragi-san said he wanted to talk to you,
so I brought him here.

12:20.000 --> 12:20.840
To me?

12:21.980 --> 12:23.590
It's about Hijirikawa Masato.

12:26.330 --> 12:28.100
Is Hijirikawa-san...

12:28.100 --> 12:32.570
Yeah. He's been equivocal
about his relationship with his father.

12:32.570 --> 12:33.980
It's exactly like you guessed.

12:35.170 --> 12:40.360
I realized after hearing her song
what it is that we're lacking.

12:40.360 --> 12:41.820
What you're lacking?

12:42.540 --> 12:44.670
Our feelings weren't as one.

12:45.820 --> 12:47.470
We've followed the same path.

12:48.850 --> 12:50.540
We loved music more than anything.

12:51.560 --> 12:53.830
And we were both saved by music.

12:53.830 --> 12:56.000
The same can be said of Hijirikawa.

12:56.410 --> 13:00.630
But he still has doubt inside him.

13:02.460 --> 13:04.290
Doubt?

13:04.760 --> 13:06.680
He hasn't steeled his resolve yet.

13:08.000 --> 13:09.810
I see.

13:11.130 --> 13:12.690
Bonds, huh?

13:38.650 --> 13:39.610
Masato-sama.

13:39.610 --> 13:41.410
How truly beautiful.

13:41.410 --> 13:42.960
He looks magnificent.

13:43.360 --> 13:46.160
He looks like the master did when he was young.

13:47.430 --> 13:50.220
The Hijirikawa family is in good hands.

13:59.680 --> 14:00.650
Hijirikawa.

14:04.310 --> 14:05.810
What are you doing here?

14:05.810 --> 14:07.970
I came as my brother's proxy.

14:07.970 --> 14:10.160
I'm here as my father's proxy.

14:10.160 --> 14:13.550
I don't believe you're
both here as their proxies.

14:13.550 --> 14:14.740
What do you want?

14:14.740 --> 14:17.030
We couldn't let your father

14:17.030 --> 14:20.630
convince you to take on
the responsibilities of the eldest son.

14:20.630 --> 14:22.380
You shouldn't have come.

14:22.380 --> 14:25.450
I may be the eldest son
of the Hijirikawa family,

14:25.450 --> 14:27.350
but I'm a member of STARISH first.

14:27.350 --> 14:30.470
Once the banquet ends,
I'll return to the others immediately.

14:30.470 --> 14:33.230
Have you discussed it with your father?

14:33.230 --> 14:34.470
Of course.

14:34.890 --> 14:40.270
Though he refused to listen and
insisted I take over the family, as usual.

14:40.270 --> 14:43.770
You couldn't call that a discussion.

14:44.480 --> 14:51.480
When you didn't hear from your father
after your year was up, you kept on running.

14:51.480 --> 14:52.340
What?

14:52.340 --> 14:57.250
That's right. You've been running
from having to make your own decision.

14:58.750 --> 15:02.680
If you return to Tokyo now,
nothing will have changed.

15:02.680 --> 15:07.270
You'll be called back here,
and your father will order you around.

15:07.270 --> 15:11.100
Your servants will beg and hope that you'll stay.

15:11.100 --> 15:14.690
And you'll continue to doubt, worry, and suffer.

15:17.980 --> 15:21.270
You haven't forgotten that time
when we were students, have you?

15:22.230 --> 15:24.860
I can't condone your lack of commitment.

15:25.570 --> 15:28.990
Why don't you show me what you can really do?

15:35.830 --> 15:40.370
I'm throwing your words right back at you now.

15:40.680 --> 15:43.630
Show me what you can really do.

15:45.510 --> 15:49.590
What you're lacking is the resolve
to follow through with what you want.

15:50.160 --> 15:53.640
If you keep running from your father,
you won't be able to sing.

15:54.930 --> 15:57.670
You don't understand how I feel.

15:57.670 --> 16:02.660
You may be the eldest son, but your
father has blessed you with freedom.

16:03.070 --> 16:06.820
Blessed me? I took it.

16:07.970 --> 16:09.860
My father was strongly opposed, too.

16:10.660 --> 16:13.960
But I couldn't stop my desire to sing.

16:14.610 --> 16:17.410
So I faced him head on.

16:18.700 --> 16:20.040
Hijirikawa.

16:20.040 --> 16:22.460
You should be able to do it now.

16:23.300 --> 16:24.290
I...

16:25.340 --> 16:28.090
This is our song.

16:34.410 --> 16:39.310
I want to be someone
who can proudly sing this song.

16:41.020 --> 16:42.640
I'm going to talk to my father.

16:42.640 --> 16:45.950
There are no doubts in my mind now.

17:05.300 --> 17:06.510
It's Masaomi-sama.

17:06.510 --> 17:08.690
I thought he was bedridden.

17:07.630 --> 17:10.490
I heard Masato-sama was here as his proxy.

17:08.990 --> 17:11.960
I hope he's feeling better...

17:12.690 --> 17:18.240
I know this is sudden,
but I'd like to announce that, as of today,

17:18.240 --> 17:22.390
my eldest son, Masato, will become
the head of the Hijirikawa family.

17:30.180 --> 17:31.250
Father!

17:36.030 --> 17:37.320
Masato.

17:37.320 --> 17:39.240
Listen to me.

17:39.240 --> 17:41.380
What are you doing up there?

17:41.860 --> 17:47.250
I'm here to announce that I will not
become the head of the Hijirikawa family.

17:50.500 --> 17:55.260
As a member of STARISH,
I will continue pursuing the path of music.

17:55.260 --> 17:56.120
What?

17:56.760 --> 17:58.250
Don't resist your fate.

17:58.670 --> 18:01.700
Your destiny was decided
long before you were born.

18:02.880 --> 18:03.850
Father.

18:04.890 --> 18:07.210
I'm not who I used to be.

18:07.880 --> 18:09.160
I've changed.

18:09.920 --> 18:11.770
Through the power of music

18:12.470 --> 18:16.070
and the wonderful bonds I share
with the members of STARISH.

18:17.440 --> 18:24.080
For me, music was once a way
to forget about reality and escape.

18:25.810 --> 18:27.510
But now it's something else.

18:28.120 --> 18:30.580
Music is what's most important to me.

18:31.230 --> 18:35.130
No one can pull me away from music anymore.

18:35.130 --> 18:41.390
But if you don't take over the family,
many people will suffer.

18:41.390 --> 18:43.100
I know that.

18:44.670 --> 18:53.480
Even if I become the object of contempt
or slander, I am prepared to bear those sins.

18:54.270 --> 18:56.080
My feelings cannot be shaken.

18:56.710 --> 18:58.960
Having reflected on myself,

18:58.960 --> 19:02.370
even if ten million people stand
in my way, I will not back down.

19:03.020 --> 19:07.540
Hear my most sincere music!

19:25.350 --> 19:29.350
Wandering aimlessly under
the weight of destiny

19:29.350 --> 19:33.350
My pack horse crushed under its weight

19:33.350 --> 19:36.610
Even as dried red leaves scatter

19:36.970 --> 19:40.820
And prepare for winter

19:40.820 --> 19:45.030
Yes, cry

19:41.580 --> 19:45.030
A harmony that blooms between those who are alike

19:45.030 --> 19:48.910
Yes, cry

19:45.870 --> 19:48.910
But today I must start with right now

19:48.910 --> 19:49.930
Lasting

19:49.930 --> 19:52.000
A song of departure

19:50.970 --> 19:52.000
Oneness

19:52.000 --> 19:53.920
A song of beginnings

19:53.070 --> 19:53.920
Lasting

19:53.920 --> 19:55.950
Let me convey to you

19:55.120 --> 19:55.950
Oneness

19:55.950 --> 19:57.340
Let me play for you

19:57.820 --> 20:04.640
With our hearts as one

20:04.640 --> 20:12.690
No matter what kind of path leads to tomorrow

20:12.690 --> 20:22.700
The seasons can't stop my heart
that has decided to pursue its dreams

20:22.700 --> 20:30.690
My song becomes the wind
and someday things will change

20:30.690 --> 20:34.830
Lasting oneness

20:58.650 --> 21:00.480
Marvelous.

21:07.990 --> 21:09.200
Father.

21:09.200 --> 21:14.320
Choosing the path of music means
severing your ties to your father.

21:14.320 --> 21:15.540
Are you sure that's what you want?

21:16.150 --> 21:18.240
I am prepared for that.

21:24.030 --> 21:29.220
Then go knowing you'll never be part
of the Hijirikawa family again!

21:29.220 --> 21:29.940
Yes, sir.

21:36.520 --> 21:39.480
Father, thank you.

21:40.440 --> 21:41.700
Thank you for everything.

21:52.620 --> 21:55.420
The song couldn't have been better.

21:55.420 --> 21:56.710
You're right.

21:56.710 --> 21:58.670
Thanks to all of you.

21:59.440 --> 22:01.720
I don't mind you when you're honest.

22:01.720 --> 22:02.810
What was that?

22:07.980 --> 22:09.150
Sir.

22:09.610 --> 22:15.680
That was the first time he looked me
in the eye and told me how he felt.

22:17.350 --> 22:25.090
His songs may someday support
millions of people throughout the world.

24:05.960 --> 24:08.100
With my love for you in my heart,

24:08.100 --> 24:09.240
I sing.

24:09.240 --> 24:10.300
Uta Pri.
